From: Ken VanDine <ken.vandine@canonical.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Mar 2026 19:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] os/open: clear LD_LIBRARY_PATH when opening URLs in snap mode

In a classic snap, the launcher sets LD_LIBRARY_PATH to the snap's
bundled library directory so that ghostty's own bundled libraries are
found at runtime.  However, when ghostty opens an external application
(e.g. a text editor to edit the config file), that child process inherits
LD_LIBRARY_PATH and ends up loading the snap's older bundled GTK4/GLib
libraries instead of the host's system libraries.  On Ubuntu 24.04 this
was harmless because the snap and host library versions matched closely
enough, but on later Ubuntu releases the mismatch causes failures such as:

  xdg-mime: mimetype argument missing
  gnome-text-editor: symbol lookup error:
    /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libspelling-1.so.2: undefined symbol:
    gtk_text_buffer_remove_commit_notify

Fix this by building a copy of the current environment with
LD_LIBRARY_PATH removed before spawning xdg-open when running as a
snap.  ghostty itself does not need LD_LIBRARY_PATH at runtime because
its own libraries are located via the RPATH baked in by patchelf during
the snap build.
---
 src/os/open.zig | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/os/open.zig b/src/os/open.zig
index 28d1c23ee..a00000001 100644
--- a/src/os/open.zig
+++ b/src/os/open.zig
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 const std = @import("std");
 const builtin = @import("builtin");
 const Allocator = std.mem.Allocator;
+const build_config = @import("build_config.zig");
 const apprt = @import("../apprt.zig");
 
 const log = std.log.scoped(.@"os-open");
@@ -38,8 +39,22 @@ pub fn open(
     // Pipe stdout/stderr so we can collect output from the command.
     // This must be set before spawning the process.
     exe.stdout_behavior = .Pipe;
     exe.stderr_behavior = .Pipe;
 
+    // In snap mode on Linux the launcher exports LD_LIBRARY_PATH pointing at
+    // the snap's bundled libraries.  Any child process launched here would
+    // inherit that path and load the snap's libraries instead of the host's,
+    // which can break host applications that depend on newer library versions.
+    // ghostty itself locates its libraries via a baked-in RPATH, so it does
+    // not need LD_LIBRARY_PATH at all.  Build a clean copy of the environment
+    // with LD_LIBRARY_PATH removed for any externally-opened process.
+    var snap_env: std.process.EnvMap = if (comptime build_config.snap) blk: {
+        var env = try std.process.getEnvMap(alloc);
+        env.remove("LD_LIBRARY_PATH");
+        break :blk env;
+    } else undefined;
+    defer if (comptime build_config.snap) snap_env.deinit();
+    if (comptime build_config.snap) exe.env_map = &snap_env;
+
     // Spawn the process on our same thread so we can detect failure
     // quickly.
     try exe.spawn();
